  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Joe Sample** (1 other source): Joe Sample was played while Al replaced his broken snare drum [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Joe Sample**: rare: 3 archived performances [7]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2001-02-03.matrix.shnf** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 10 songs; 75 min; rated 5/5 by 5 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer calls the recording nearly perfect; attendee heard smooth jams, voice-box guitar from Krasno and deep Hammond [4]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Casey Benjamin joined the band on saxophone for part of the show [1]\n- The show came from the second Soulive/Project Logic tour [2]\n- The Project Logic set from this night is also available at archive.org [2]\n- A horn player sat in with the band, and Project Logic opened the night [3]\n- Reviewer ranks this show, with a 2004 Tribeca Rock Club recording, among the best Soulive performances to own [4]\n- Show took place a couple of months before Soulive opened the Dave Matthews summer tour; their angular sound was toned down and refined [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2001-02-03.matrix.shnf**: taped by Peter Costello; source: Schoeps CMC621 + SBD > Mackie 1202 > Apogee AD1000 > Tascam DA-P1 [1]. Also: The recording is tracked so the whole show fits on a single 80-minute disc; Peter Costello recorded this show [1][3]",
